completed_at: "2026-11-17T09:04:47.334Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "credential_key_assignment judges a value by the literal left once run-time references expand to nothing, so a literal before or after a reference and a literal default are refused in text, quoted-key and object-payload spellings; A bare ${API_KEY}, $(op read key), <placeholder> and an empty default stay allowed, and one documented bare-$VAR policy applies to both password_assignment and credential_key_assignment; The pm-1l85at false-positive corpus and the pm-gh1704 must-allow corpus stay clean and the linear-time controls still pass"
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "secret-rules.ts: CREDENTIAL_VALUE captures a value whole when it holds a run-time reference (braced, command, dollar-name or angle placeholder) or opens with a quoted piece concatenated to more text; the literal left once references expand is judged as data by CREDENTIAL_LITERAL_VALUE, the unchanged reference-free grammar, through the new declarative SecretRule.literalValue field, with minimumLiteralLength 8 and entropy measured on the literal. Bounds: at most 64 literal characters before the first reference, whitespace-free references and quoted pieces, repeated groups bounded at 4096 and quoted pieces at 4. The expansion walker reads a dollar-name reference: CONSTANT_CASE names expand to nothing, a bare name (the whole value, quoted or not, judged on the source) spells nothing, any other dollar text is literal; this one policy applies to password_assignment and credential_key_assignment alike. Documented in docs/MUTATION_INTEGRITY.md."
expected_result: "A literal before or after a reference and a literal default are refused under a credential key in text, quoted-key, element, escaped and payload spellings, while bare references, bare variables, empty defaults and literals that are paths, URLs or words stay clean, and both key-named rules agree on a bare variable"
actual_result: "secret-guard-credential-references-and-names.spec.ts passes (65 cases incl. linear-time controls) together with the GH-1704, GH-1699 and whole-value-reference corpora (723 tests across the security suites), check-secrets is clean, both changed files are 100% covered, pnpm quality:static passes, and the tracker false-positive scan over 47,292 texts is unchanged at 8 and 4 hits; on main 94773473b the 21 must-flag rows and the policy test fail"
component: secret-guard
